      "matches": [
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": "A Samsung Galaxy XR (`SM-I610`, `xrvst2ue`, build `I610UEU2AZF3`, kernel 5.10.240) was rooted from an"
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "unprivileged `adb shell` (`uid=2000(shell)`, SELinux Enforcing, locked bootloader) by porting the"
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": "GhostLock (CVE-2026-43499) kernel LPE. The result is a stable `uid=0(root)` context"
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "(`u:r:kernel:s0`, SELinux permissive), reproducible across a full reboot, with no flashing and no"
        },
        {
          "line": 119,
          "text": "root umh result wake=1 complete=1 retval=0 socket=1"
        },
        {
          "line": 131,
          "text": "uid=0(root) gid=0(root) groups=0(root) context=u:r:kernel:s0"
        },
        {
          "line": 134,
          "text": "Permissive"
        },
        {
          "line": 142,
          "text": "Tested several times from cold boots (SELinux Enforcing each time): push, run, verify \u2192"
        },
        {
          "line": 143,
          "text": "`uid=0(root)` every time, no reboot. A reboot clears root (SELinux back to Enforcing); re-run the"
        },
        {
          "line": 166,
          "text": "flashing, no on-disk changes); a reboot fully clears it. Do not use on any device you do not own."
        }
      ]
    },
